WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

light-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Galaxies sit inside gas too faint to see

light-2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
A light behind reveals it

cells-3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
A few cells make most of the absorption

dip-1
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Each gas cell leaves a shadow

dip-2
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Moving gas shifts its shadow, like a siren

dip-3
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Amount sets how much light is taken

dip-4
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Heat spreads it out

sum-1
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Dozens of shadows merge into a few dips

sum-2
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Motion, not heat, makes this width

saturation-2
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Once black, only wider

lsf-1
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.000
A blurry telescope merges dips

lsf-2
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Blur turns black dips grey

noise-1
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Longer exposures beat the noise

fit-1
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:48.000
We fit a few clouds

fit-2
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
The total O VI survives

fit-3
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:01.000
The clouds are not the cells

yourturn-1
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Now it is yours. Same galaxy, same beam
